  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 13-layer planar multilayer stack on Al substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr, HfO2, SiO2, Cr (13 finite layers). All layer thicknesses bounded to [30, 300] nm. Wavelength bands: 400-700 nm (maximize absorptance, minimize reflectance), 700-2000 nm (maximize reflectance). Normal incidence, unpolarized light. Use L-BFGS-B constrained quasi-Newton optimizer with gradient clipping. Initialize thicknesses at 80 nm for Cr layers and 120 nm for dielectric layers. Total layer count constraint: exactly 13 finite layers. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 400-700 nm, 700-2000 nm. soft objectives: high absorptance in 400-700 nm; low reflectance in 400-700 nm; high reflectance in 700-2000 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflectance in 400-700 nm; high absorptance in 700-2000 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count not exceeding 20.",
